      "side": 1,
      "message": "Okay so Brian and I were talking about what it would look like to have a \"Surface Spec\" type object that describes everything about the properties of a surface (i.e. things needed to create the surface) besides size and ids. This spec would be used for various functionality queries (texturable, renderable, etc.), start to replace SkSurfaceCharacterization for ddls, and in general be one struct that we can pass around throughout Ganesh, whether proxy or real surface, that we can always use to know the properties of a surface. I.E. every proxy, surface, backend surface, characterization, etc. will all have a GrSurfaceSpec object.\n\nThis CL is less of a real CL and more of a way to hack out some ideas and see what they look like in code before diving too deep into such a new approach. Just wanted to start to get y\u0027alls high level thoughts at this point (I personally find it very hard to write (at least quickly) tons of structs in a design doc and have someone reading it be able to follow them).",
      "revId": "8a44b84092e397bf70ef7dc694291e980706417f",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
