      "side": 1,
      "message": "So D3D has an issue where if we are outside of core GrD3D* code we all include in GrD3DTypesMinimal.h which does not include d3d12.h which includes windows.h.\n\nThese structs have d3d specific values in them so they should live in GrD3DTypes.h. However, with the current way I have things set up that would mean where ever GrSurfaceSpec lives (probably GrTypes.h) would have to include GrD3DTypes.h since we need the size of the struct. Then that brings in windows.h which messes up all our code.\n\nJim any thoughts on how to get around this or how to set up this code to make it happier?",
